## Main risks & assumptions
1. **Stripe Terminal SDK** requires certified hardware; procurement lead time not included.
2. Supplier APIs may have rate limits or require NDA-gated credentials; integration scope assumes REST/JSON.
3. Multi-tenant RLS adds query complexity; performance testing under concurrent load is essential.
4. Real-time KDS latency target (<500 ms) must be validated in a load test before go-live.

**Delivery range:** 14–18 weeks · 230–260 h


--- Example 2 — Mobile app for field technicians with offline sync ---

Project description:
A facilities management company needs a React Native app for Android tablets used by
field technicians. Technicians must be able to consult and update work orders, attach
photos and signatures, and log parts used against an asset register. The app must work
fully offline and sync when connectivity is restored. The backend is an existing Django
REST API; the app only needs to integrate with it.

Estimation:

# Estimation: Field Technician Mobile App (React Native + Offline Sync)

## Executive summary
React Native application targeting Android tablets with a robust offline-first
architecture. The main complexity is the conflict-resolution strategy for concurrent
edits and the binary asset (photos) sync pipeline.

---

