## Main risks & assumptions
1. Conflict resolution strategy (last-write-wins) must be validated with the product owner; business rules may require manual merge for some fields.
2. Django API must expose `updated_at` timestamps on all synced resources; backend changes are not in scope.
3. Barcode scanning accuracy depends on tablet camera quality; a fallback manual-entry path is included.

**Delivery range:** 10–13 weeks · 140–160 h


--- Example 3 — E-commerce analytics data pipeline ---

Project description:
An online retailer wants to consolidate data from Shopify, Google Ads, and Meta Ads
into a single data warehouse (BigQuery). They need nightly ETL jobs that compute
cohort-based LTV, CAC by channel, and weekly retention curves. A lightweight BI
dashboard (Metabase) must surface the KPIs to the marketing team with self-service
filtering. Alerting when CAC exceeds a configurable threshold.

Estimation:

# Estimation: E-Commerce Analytics Data Pipeline

## Executive summary
Cloud-native ELT pipeline on BigQuery with three source connectors, a dbt transformation
layer for business metrics, and a Metabase BI layer. The CAC/LTV models require careful
attribution logic alignment with the marketing team before implementation.

---

## Breakdown by module

### 1. Data Ingestion (ELT Connectors)
| Task | Hours | Profile | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Shopify connector (orders, customers, products) via Airbyte | 8h | Data Engineer | Airbyte Cloud |
| Google Ads connector (campaigns, ad groups, spend) | 4h | Data Engineer | Native Airbyte connector |
| Meta Ads connector (campaigns, spend, impressions) | 4h | Data Engineer | Native Airbyte connector |
| Raw landing zone schema design in BigQuery | 6h | Data Engineer | |
| Incremental sync strategy + deduplication | 8h | Data Engineer | |
| **Subtotal** | **30h** | | |

### 2. dbt Transformation Layer
| Task | Hours | Profile | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Staging models (clean + type-cast raw data) | 8h | Analytics Engineer | |
| Intermediate models: unified customer timeline | 12h | Analytics Engineer | |
| LTV model (cohort-based, 30/60/90-day windows) | 16h | Analytics Engineer | |
| CAC model (blended + by channel, attribution: last-click) | 12h | Analytics Engineer | |
| Retention curve model (weekly cohorts) | 12h | Analytics Engineer | |
| dbt tests (not_null, unique, accepted_values, relationships) | 8h | Analytics Engineer | |
| **Subtotal** | **68h** | | |

### 3. Orchestration
| Task | Hours | Profile | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cloud Composer (Airflow) DAG setup, nightly schedule | 8h | Data Engineer | |
| Failure alerting + Slack webhook notifications | 4h | Data Engineer | |
| Backfill strategy for historical data (18 months) | 4h | Data Engineer | |
| **Subtotal** | **16h** | | |

### 4. BI Dashboard (Metabase)
| Task | Hours | Profile | Notes |
